<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 6 September, from 394 to 1966.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/394">394 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,632 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Theodosius I defeats Eugenius at the Frigidus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor Theodosius defeated the usurper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eugenius">Eugenius</a>, backed by the pagan senatorial aristocracy, in a two-day battle in the Julian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>. Traditional Roman religion lost its last political champion.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1522">1522 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">504 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Victoria completes the first voyage around the world</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Victoria, last survivor of Magellan's five ships, reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> under Juan Sebastián Elcano with 18 men. The voyage revealed the vast size of the Pacific and the true scale of the globe.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1628">1628 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">398 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Endecott's Puritans arrive at Salem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-endecott">John Endecott</a> landed at Naumkeag with Puritan settlers, taking charge of the small settlement soon renamed Salem. It became the first town of the Massachusetts Bay Colony.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1901">1901 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">125 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">President McKinley is shot in Buffalo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Anarchist Leon Czolgosz shot <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-mckinley">William McKinley</a> twice at the Pan-American Exposition. The president died eight days later, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodore-roosevelt">Theodore Roosevelt</a> succeeded him.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1966">1966 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">60 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hendrik Verwoerd is stabbed to death in parliament</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>'s prime minister, chief architect of apartheid, was killed in the House of Assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-town">Cape Town</a> by parliamentary messenger Dimitri Tsafendas. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apartheid">Apartheid</a> continued under his successors.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li></ol>
